       <h1>Arabian Aces finalize squad for Abu Dhabi T10</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Head coach Lance Klusener has finalized the Arabian Aces squad for the upcoming Abu Dhabi T10 tournament, held from November 7 to November 20 at Zayed Cricket Stadium. The team, owned by a consortium led by Pankaj and Neeraj Jain, features international stars Moeen Ali, Andre Russell, and Liam Livingstone.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/arabian-aces-finalize-squad-for-abu-dhabi-t10.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Klusener emphasized that the T10 format requires innovation and advanced problem-solving skills, noting that his squad is built to balance aggressive batting with disciplined bowling. The franchise completed its draft process on October 1, 2026, and is now preparing for the explosive, short-format competition.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively summarizes the squad assembly and coach's comments, though it misses the full squad list provided in the source.</p>
