       <h1>‘Behemoth!’ to Close Newport Beach Film Festival</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The 27th annual Newport Beach Film Festival will conclude on October 22 with the screening of &quot;Behemoth!&quot; Writer and director Tony Gilroy is scheduled to attend the event. The film stars Pedro Pascal as Alex Serian, a gifted cellist returning to Los Angeles after two decades of touring.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/behemoth-to-close-newport-beach-film-festival.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Serian’s homecoming serves as the catalyst for a life-changing personal adventure. The festival’s choice of this film for the closing night highlights the narrative of a performer reconnecting with his roots after a long career on the road.</p>
