       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Captain Smit Machchhar Hailed for Saving 174 Lives During Mid-Air Emergency</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Captain Smit Machchhar is being celebrated across India for his heroism aboard flydubai Flight FZ1073. Despite sustaining serious injuries during a cockpit attack, Machchhar displayed remarkable presence of mind to land the aircraft safely in Tabuk, Saudi Arabia, protecting all 174 passengers and crew.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/captain-smit-machchhar-hailed-for-saving-174-lives-during-mi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>President Droupadi Murmu, Vice-President C P Radhakrishnan, and various Union ministers have praised his courage, professionalism, and dedication to duty. Leaders emphasized that his decisive actions prevented a catastrophic tragedy. The nation continues to express gratitude for his service and has offered well-wishes for his recovery following the mid-air crisis.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately captures the core facts, names, and the specific individuals involved in the incident as reported.</p>
