     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Cockroach Janta Party Plans Mumbai Protest Demanding CEC Resignation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke announced a protest at Mumbai’s Shivaji Park on October 2 to demand the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. Dipke alleged that 13 crore voters have been deleted from rolls since 2024 to favor the ruling government, and he warned of further protests if demands are not met.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/cockroach-janta-party-plans-mumbai-protest-demanding-cec-res.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The group is also calling for criminal charges against Kumar and a return to paper ballots, citing security concerns regarding Electronic Voting Machines. Despite Mumbai police denying permission for the demonstration, Dipke stated the party intends to proceed with protests across six additional cities, culminating in a final demonstration at Jantar Mantar in New Delhi.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately covers the key details of the protest, including the time, location, and the founder's specific demands and rhetoric.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/mumbai/cjp-to-protest-against-cec-in-mumbai-on-october-2-dipke-challenges-cm-fadnavis/article71533827.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-01/cockroach-janta-party-plans-mumbai-protest-demanding-cec-res" data-title="Cockroach Janta Party Plans Mumbai Protest Demanding CEC Resignation"><b>Share:</b>
