      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/science">science</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="science">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · Phys.org · 2026-10-01 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Dutch farmers pilot rice cultivation to combat peatland sinking</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Farmer Sander Roeleveld is piloting rice cultivation in the Netherlands to address environmental concerns regarding sinking peatlands. Roughly one-tenth of the country is peatland, which releases carbon dioxide and subsides when drained for cattle grazing. Researchers hope that keeping fields wet for rice will mitigate this land subsidence and reduce greenhouse gas emissions, which account for 2-3% of national totals.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/dutch-farmers-pilot-rice-cultivation-to-combat-peatland-sink.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The pilot project involves 0.6 hectares and 30 international rice cultivars to test viability in the temperate Dutch climate. While historically focused on dairy, researchers and farmers are exploring alternative wetland agriculture to protect the low-lying nation's future.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is accurate but leaves out significant source material, including the goal to produce three tonnes of rice and the specific mention of sushi/risotto applications.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://phys.org/news/2026-10-rice-dutch-crop-peatlands.html" rel="noopener">Phys.org</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
