     <article class="story single" data-beat="environment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Guardian Environment · 2026-10-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>El Niño Wildfires Devastate Indonesian Orangutan Habitats</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#El Niño</span> <span>#Indonesia</span> <span>#Wildfires</span> <span>#Orangutans</span></div>
       <p>Indonesia's ape heartlands are experiencing devastating infernos, triggered by the global climate phenomenon El Niño. These widespread wildfires are consuming vast tracts of Indonesia's forests and peatland, leading to significant environmental impact. The long-term consequences for the affected animal populations remain undetermined.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/el-nino-wildfires-devastate-indonesian-orangutan-habitats.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The fires have had a direct and severe impact on local wildlife. Rescuers last month saved an orangutan pair, a mother named Mama Abu and her eight-month-old baby, Abu, from the blazes. They were discovered in an oil palm subsidiary estate. Mama Abu reportedly suffered from peeling hands due to walking on scorched ground, while her infant was found dehydrated and thin.</p><p>Beyond the immediate threat to individual animals, the ongoing wildfires are unleashing thick smog across the region. Critically, these infernos are actively destroying the natural habitat of some of the planet's most vulnerable species, highlighting the extensive ecological damage.</p><p>What to watch: Efforts to contain wildfires and assess long-term ecological impacts.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is concise, accurate, and captures all key details from the source without padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/01/el-nino-orangutans-indonesia-wildlife-destruction-aoe" rel="noopener">Guardian Environment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
