     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Flydubai Boeing 737 MAX Survives Extreme Dive After Co-Pilot Attack</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Flydubai</span> <span>#Boeing 737 MAX</span> <span>#Aviation Safety</span> <span>#Pilot</span></div>
       <p>A Flydubai Boeing 737 MAX, carrying 180 passengers, endured a steep dive lasting over a minute, significantly exceeding its maximum tolerance and safe operating parameters, yet managed to land safely. This outcome has been widely described as a &quot;miracle&quot; by pilots on social media, who based their observations on publicly available flight-tracking data. The aircraft reportedly clipped 30,000 feet per minute in its descent.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/flydubai-boeing-737-max-survives-extreme-dive-after-co-pilot.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Upon landing, visuals revealed that the rudders attached to the vertical stabiliser had been ripped off, underscoring the extreme forces the aircraft experienced. Media reports indicate that the incident followed an attack by the Omani co-pilot on Indian pilot Captain Smit Machchha with a crash axe, whose actions during the crisis have been broadly praised. An American pilot quoted by author Buzz Patterson stated the aircraft exceeded its maximum operating speed by 100 knots.</p><p>The survival of the 737 MAX is particularly notable given the aircraft's history of two prior crashes involving uncommanded nose-down maneuvers, which resulted in aircraft disintegration. In contrast, the Flydubai plane remained intact. A C-17 military pilot praised the 737 MAX’s structural integrity, calling it &quot;genuinely a testament to the 737 MAX and modern carbon composite airframes,&quot; highlighting its specialized aluminum alloys and advanced composites.</p><p>What to watch: Ongoing investigations into the incident and its implications for aviation safety.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the reporting on the Flydubai incident, maintaining factual accuracy regarding the technical details and expert commentary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/flydubai-plane-survived-near-supersonic-dive-at-30000-ft-per-minute-why-the-boeing-737-max-didnt-break-apart-10363297.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-01/flydubai-boeing-737-max-survives-extreme-dive-after-co-pilot" data-title="Flydubai Boeing 737 MAX Survives Extreme Dive After Co-Pilot Attack"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
