     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>High-Level Committee Seeks Extensive Religion-Wise Demographic Data</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Ministry of Home Affairs-constituted High-Level Committee on Demographic Changes (HLCDC), chaired by Justice Prakash Prabhakar Naolekar, has issued a 35-point questionnaire to State governments. The committee, tasked with studying demographic shifts from illegal immigration and ‘abnormal’ reasons, is seeking religion-wise data on voter registrations, school enrolment, vehicle ownership, and property transactions covering the last 15 years.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/high-level-committee-seeks-extensive-religion-wise-demograph.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>State officials have expressed concern, noting that administrative databases do not currently classify citizens by religion across these categories. The committee, which is also evaluating institutional mechanisms for population stabilisation, has one year to submit its findings, with a possible six-month extension.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a concise and accurate summary of the committee's mandate, the questionnaire details, and the challenges faced by states.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/conundrum-over-panels-questionnaire-seeking-extensive-data-on-demographic-changes-explained/article71523595.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
