     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>ICC Reveals 2027 World Cup Schedule, India to Face Australia on October 7</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#ICC World Cup</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Australia</span></div>
       <p>The International Cricket Council (ICC) has announced the full schedule for the 2027 ODI World Cup, which will be co-hosted by South Africa, Zimbabwe, and Namibia. The tournament is set to commence on October 7, 2027, with 2023 World Cup finalists India and Australia clashing in Cape Town.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/icc-reveals-2027-world-cup-schedule-india-to-face-australia-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>India has been placed in Group A, alongside arch-rivals Pakistan, defending champions Australia, Afghanistan, co-hosts Zimbabwe, and a qualifier team. A highly anticipated match between India and Pakistan is scheduled for October 10 in Johannesburg.</p><p>Group B comprises co-hosts South Africa, England, New Zealand, Sri Lanka, Bangladesh, and another qualifier team. The tournament structure includes a Super Seven stage, running from October 25 to November 14, where the top seven teams will compete. The top four from this stage will advance to the semi-finals, culminating in the final on November 21, 2027, in Johannesburg.</p><p>What to watch: Teams will need to win 13 games to secure the tournament trophy.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is accurate and captures the essential schedule details provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/icc-odi-world-cup-2027-schedule-announcement-live-updates-india-vs-pakistan-12124886#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
