       <h1>India Honors Pilot Smit Machchhar After Mid-Flight Attack</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Captain Smit Machchhar is being hailed as a hero after surviving a stabbing by his co-pilot during a flydubai flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv. Despite his injuries, Machchhar helped secure the cockpit, allowing others to restrain the attacker and ensuring the safe emergency landing of 174 passengers in Tabuk, Saudi Arabia.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/india-honors-pilot-smit-machchhar-after-mid-flight-attack.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In recognition of his bravery, the Gujarat government announced the 'Gujarat Gaurav Puraskar' award. Across India, temples have organized special prayers and havans for the pilot, who remains in stable condition following surgery in Saudi Arabia.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the key events, the honors bestowed upon the pilot, and the global reactions reported in the source.</p>
