       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Pilot Smit Machchhar Recovering After Foiling Cockpit Attack</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Indian Ambassador to the UAE Deepak Mittal confirmed that Captain Smit Machchhar is in good health and recovering well after being stabbed by his co-pilot aboard Flydubai flight FZ1073. The incident occurred on Wednesday during a flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv, forcing an emergency landing in Tabuk, Saudi Arabia.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/indian-pilot-smit-machchhar-recovering-after-foiling-cockpit.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Machchhar, who was transferred to the UAE for further care, sustained serious injuries while preventing his co-pilot from crashing the plane. The co-pilot, identified as an Omani national, reportedly sent the aircraft into a rapid descent before Machchhar regained control. All 174 passengers arrived safely in Israel following the intervention.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively synthesizes the source material, capturing the incident, the pilot's recovery, and the specific details regarding the flight and emergency landing.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/recovering-well-indian-envoy-to-uae-says-captain-smit-machchhar-is-in-good-health-10363407.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
