     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Pilots Including Smit Machchhar Save Passengers in Mid-Air Crises</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#positive</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Captain Smit Machchhar was stabbed by his co-pilot on flydubai flight FZ1073 from Dubai to Tel Aviv on September 30, 2026, causing the Boeing 737 MAX 8 to plunge over 14,000 feet in 29 seconds. Wounded on the cockpit floor, Machchhar opened the door, allowing passengers and crew to overpower the attacker before landing safely in Tabuk, Saudi Arabia. Other notable Indian pilot interventions include Captain Monica Khanna safely landing a SpiceJet flight after an engine fire in Patna, and Captain Iqrom Rifadly Fahmi Zainal circling Tiruchirappalli for hours after a landing-gear failure.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/indian-pilots-including-smit-machchhar-save-passengers-in-mi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Additional historical cases highlight medical emergencies handled by Indian flight commanders. Air India captains A.K. Singh and J.S. Gill executed international diversions to Toronto and Stockholm respectively in late 2010 to save passengers suffering from cardiac arrests. Furthermore, Captain R.S. Attari diverted a Kochi-Delhi flight to Bengaluru on December 17 after a passenger experienced severe giddiness. Each incident demonstrates how prompt pilot decisions across nearly 16 years successfully brought passengers to safety or medical care.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is comprehensive and effectively summarizes the multiple historical cases provided in the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/changemakers/smit-machchhar-indian-pilots-saved-lives-mid-air-12613537" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
