       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-01 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ivanna Lisette Ortiz indicted for attempted murder at Rihanna's home</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A Florida woman, 36-year-old Ivanna Lisette Ortiz, has been indicted by a Los Angeles grand jury on 14 felony counts, including attempted murder, following a March 8 shooting at the home of Rihanna and A$AP Rocky. Authorities allege Ortiz fired at least 20 rounds from an AR-15-style rifle at the property, striking a trailer and a nursery where the couple's children were present.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/ivanna-lisette-ortiz-indicted-for-attempted-murder-at-rihann.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>No injuries were reported. After a judge ruled Ortiz mentally competent to stand trial, the case is now on a fast track. Ortiz is currently held on $2.6 million bail and has entered a not guilty plea.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is missing important details provided in the source text, specifically the names of the children, the mention of Rihanna's mother, and the context regarding the defendant's profession.</p>
