       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mumbai Neighbors Hail Flydubai Pilot Smit Machchhar as Hero</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Mumbai residents in Chembur and Ghatkopar are celebrating Flydubai Captain Smit Machchhar, who survived an alleged mid-air attack by his co-pilot on a flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv. The Boeing 737 MAX 8 diverted to Tabuk, Saudi Arabia, after the co-pilot attempted to crash the aircraft; Machchhar reportedly fought back, allowing the crew to neutralize the attacker.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/mumbai-neighbors-hail-flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar-as-hero.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Currently recovering from surgery in stable condition, the 39-year-old pilot is being lauded by Prime Minister Narendra Modi and local officials. Neighbors describe the former SpiceJet captain as a focused, calm professional, and are planning a major celebration for his eventual return to Mumbai.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively summarizes the community reaction and the pilot's background as detailed in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/cities/mumbai-news/flydubai-pilot-smit-machchhar-as-his-neighbours-know-him-calm-aviation-obsessed-10361951.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
