      <a href="/stats">Stats</a>
      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/space">space</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="space">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPACE</span> · NASA · 2026-10-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NASA’s SpaceX Crew-13 Launches to International Space Station</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NASA</span> <span>#SpaceX</span> <span>#ISS</span> <span>#Spaceflight</span></div>
       <p>On October 1, 2026, the NASA-led SpaceX Crew-13 mission successfully launched aboard a Falcon 9 rocket and Dragon spacecraft from Space Launch Complex 40 at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida. This launch initiates a long-duration science mission to the International Space Station (ISS), carrying a diverse, international crew.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/nasas-spacex-crew-13-launches-to-international-space-station.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The four-person crew includes NASA astronauts Jessica Watkins and Luke Delaney, alongside CSA (Canadian Space Agency) astronaut Joshua Kutryk, and Roscosmos cosmonaut Sergey Teteryatnikov. These astronauts and cosmonauts are embarking on a critical mission to conduct scientific research and maintain the orbital outpost, contributing to global space exploration efforts.</p><p>The Dragon spacecraft is anticipated to dock with the International Space Station at 7 p.m. EDT. NASA will provide extensive live coverage of Crew-13’s arrival, with the agency’s broadcast set to begin at 5:20 p.m. EDT across multiple digital platforms. The mission highlights ongoing international collaboration in human spaceflight and scientific discovery.</p><p>What to watch: Tune into NASA’s live broadcast of Crew-13’s docking at the ISS starting at 5:20 p.m. EDT at https://www.nasa.gov/live.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately incorporates all provided source details, including the crew names, launch location, and specific timing for the docking and broadcast.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.nasa.gov/image-article/nasas-spacex-crew-13-launches/" rel="noopener">NASA</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
