     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pilot Smit Machchhar Hailed as Hero After Surviving Mid-Air Stabbing</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Captain Smit Machchhar has received global praise from leaders including President Droupadi Murmu, Prime Minister Narendra Modi, Benjamin Netanyahu, and Donald Trump. On September 30, 2026, Machchhar was stabbed mid-air by his co-pilot on flydubai flight FZ1073, causing the aircraft carrying 174 passengers to drop nearly 14,000 feet in under 30 seconds. Despite bleeding on the cockpit floor, Machchhar activated the door release so passengers and off-duty pilots could overpower the attacker and land safely in Tabuk, Saudi Arabia.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/pilot-smit-machchhar-hailed-as-hero-after-surviving-mid-air-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Machchhar is currently recovering in a Tabuk hospital. A former SpiceJet line training captain who joined flydubai in 2022, Machchhar found aviation later in life after studying textile engineering and management at Mumbai's Welingkar Institute. Authorities are actively investigating the co-pilot's motive behind the cockpit attack.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is well-written and incorporates the specific details provided in the full source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/smit-machchhar-flydubai-pilot-who-is-he/article71531666.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
