       <h1>Putin Warns Nuclear Weapons Use Cannot Be Ruled Out Amid Escalating Tensions</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#World</span> <span>#Politics</span> <span>#Nuclear Weapons</span> <span>#Russia</span></div>
       <p>Russian President Vladimir Putin warned on Thursday that the world cannot be certain nuclear weapons will never be used, emphasizing the increasing risks associated with powerful armaments. Speaking at the Valdai Discussion Club forum in Moscow, Putin stated, “If a gun is hanging on the stage, sooner or later it must go off,” underscoring the potential for catastrophic global consequences from the leading powers' arsenals.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/putin-warns-nuclear-weapons-use-cannot-be-ruled-out-amid-esc.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Putin cautioned that escalating conflicts could rapidly reach a point of no return, attributing this dangerous trajectory to “arrogance and overconfidence.” He urged countries to avoid such a fatal threshold, highlighting that the moment when changes become impossible may arrive unexpectedly.</p><p>His remarks coincided with heightened warnings from Moscow regarding the Russian exclave of Kaliningrad, situated between NATO members Poland and Lithuania. Putin asserted that Russia would consider deploying “all weapons at its disposal” in the event of a direct attack on Kaliningrad or any other Russian territory.</p><p>While stating Russia has no plans to attack European countries and desires peaceful coexistence, Putin characterized NATO as an adversary larger than Russia. These comments come amidst ongoing tensions between Moscow and Western nations over the conflict in Ukraine.</p><p>What to watch: Further statements from global leaders regarding nuclear de-escalation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively summarizes Putin's statements and the context regarding Kalining the context of the Valdai Discussion Club and Kaliningrad warnings.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/sooner-or-later-it-must-go-off-putin-says-world-cannot-rule-out-nuclear-weapons-use-ws-l-10363626.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
