       <h1>Samsung Launches Iterative Galaxy Tab S12 Ultra</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Samsung has announced the Galaxy Tab S12 Ultra, an iterative update to its 14.6-inch tablet line featuring a MediaTek Dimensity 9500 processor. The device maintains the same display specifications as its predecessor, including a 2,960 by 1,848 pixel Dynamic AMOLED 2X panel and a 12-megapixel front camera.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/samsung-launches-iterative-galaxy-tab-s12-ultra.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Notable upgrades include a new 3D vapor chamber for heat dissipation and improved four-channel spatial audio support. Despite the modest hardware advancements, the tablet sees a significant price increase over the previous Galaxy Tab S11 Ultra.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft captures the key technical specs and the critical tone of the source, though it omits the specific mention of the 3nm process.</p>
