       <h1>Scotland Coach Pocognoli Targets First Win Against North Macedonia</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Scotland head coach Sebastien Pocognoli seeks his first victory as his team prepares to face North Macedonia in a Nations League Group B1 match on Saturday. Following a draw with Slovenia and a 3-0 loss to Switzerland, Pocognoli faces tactical decisions, including replacing the suspended Jack Hendry.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/scotland-coach-pocognoli-targets-first-win-against-north-mac.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The manager may maintain his three-at-the-back system despite the recent defeat. Potential lineup adjustments include considering debuts for Luke Graham and the possible return of Aaron Hickey to the starting XI. The match takes place in Skopje, where Scotland aims to rebound against the lowest-ranked side in their group.</p>
