     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · BS Personal Finance · 2026-10-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>TCS Acquires Best Buy's India GCC, Eyes AI-Native Development</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Personal Finance</span> <span>#Technology</span> <span>#Business</span> <span>#AI</span></div>
       <p>Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) has announced its acquisition of US consumer electronics retailer Best Buy’s global capability centre (GCC) in India. While the financial terms remain undisclosed, this multi-year agreement will see Best Buy’s India entity transition to TCS, ensuring business continuity while focusing on its transformation into an AI-native centre.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/tcs-acquires-best-buys-india-gcc-eyes-ai-native-development.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>For an ordinary saver or taxpayer, this move signifies a strategic shift in how large corporations leverage technology and talent. TCS aims to combine the Best Buy centre’s retail and enterprise knowledge with its own expertise in technology, engineering, and artificial intelligence to accelerate innovation and scale AI-powered solutions. Krishnan Ramanujam, president of TCS’ consumer business group, highlighted the goal of creating an “AI-native capability engine” that could benefit the broader retail industry.</p><p>This acquisition reflects a trend where some GCCs in India, facing maturation challenges, are being sold to service providers like TCS, which are actively expanding their revenue streams in this sector. Ahrey Smith, vice-president of technology strategy and transformation at Best Buy, emphasized TCS’s understanding of the team’s value and its technological capabilities.</p><p>Essentially, this means that the jobs and operations within Best Buy's India tech hub will now be managed by TCS, with a strong focus on developing advanced AI solutions for retail. It's a business-to-business transaction that could lead to more efficient, AI-driven retail experiences down the line.</p><p>What to watch: The impact of this AI-native centre on future retail technology and consumer experiences.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reports the acquisition and the strategic intent behind the transition of the India GCC to TCS.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/tcs-to-buy-us-retailer-best-buy-s-india-gcc-develop-an-ai-native-centre-126100101559_1.html" rel="noopener">BS Personal Finance</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
