       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Yami Gautam Addresses Oscar Speculation at Nayyi Navelli Trailer Launch</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Yami Gautam attended the Mumbai trailer launch for her upcoming film, Nayyi Navelli, marking her first major public appearance since winning a National Award. She was joined by cast members Adinath Kothare, Sushmita Mukherjee, and Mita Vashisht, alongside producers Nikhil Madhok, Aanand L Rai, and Himanshu Sharma and director Balaji Mohan.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-01/yami-gautam-addresses-oscar-speculation-at-nayyi-navelli-tra.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the event, Gautam addressed media speculation regarding a potential Oscar campaign following her recent award win. Responding to inquiries about her future ambitions, the actress stated, “Aapke sapne sirf aapko pata hone chahiye,” emphasizing that personal dreams should remain private as she continues her career trajectory.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is concise and accurately reflects the provided source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/nayyi-navelli-trailer-launch-is-yami-gautam-aiming-for-an-oscar-after-national-award-win-actress-breaks-silence-aapke-sapne-sirf-aapko-pata-hone-chahiye/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
